WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:06.466 --> 00:00:10.000
Sport has the power to connect people everywhere.

cue-2
00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.240
But that connection must also be protected online.

cue-3
00:00:14.466 --> 00:00:18.842
Tackling online abuse is a responsibility across sport.

cue-4
00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:22.186
Recognising online abuse is the first step.

cue-5
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.440
Knowing how to respond turns awareness into action.

cue-6
00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:30.133
And that knowledge matters to everyone in sport - not only experts.

cue-7
00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:36.240
That is why the FlA's United Against Online Abuse initiative developed

cue-8
00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:39.933
the UAOA eLearning Course: a practical learning experience

cue-9
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:45.840
for understanding and responding to online abuse in sport.

cue-10
00:00:45.866 --> 00:00:49.133
Developed in collaboration with Notre Dame University

cue-11
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:53.400
along with the FIA Member Clubs and academic partners in Spain,

cue-12
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.147
Czechia, Sweden and Slovenia, it brings together research,

cue-13
00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.281
education and real-world perspectives.

cue-14
00:01:00.621 --> 00:01:03.629
The course starts by understanding online abuse

cue-15
00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.971
and recognising its human impact.

cue-16
00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:11.254
It then looks at how harm spreads, your rights and responsibilities,

cue-17
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.900
and how to take action.

cue-18
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.919
Understand the issue.

cue-19
00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:16.319
Know how to respond.

cue-20
00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:19.800
Because a safer sporting environment

cue-21
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.066
starts with informed action - from all of us.

cue-22
00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.090
Everyone has a role to play

cue-23
00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:28.114
Start the course
